cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as a theoretical research preprint."
title: "Tame Moduli of Life: Sharp O-Minimal Finiteness for Repair-Closed Systems and Tropical Walls over the Landscape of Physical Laws"
authors:
  - family-names: Debnath
    given-names: Devanik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8310-6921"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-31"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Devanik21/The-Invention-Archive"
abstract: >-
  A conditional finiteness framework for finite-dimensional families of
  repair-closed systems. The paper encodes a model-relative life-admissibility
  predicate in a fixed o-minimal structure, derives finite connected-component
  conclusions and sharp format-degree bounds under additional hypotheses,
  and compares the resulting tame partition with tropical candidate walls.
  A synthetic semialgebraic example is supplied; no empirical or universal
  biological claim is made.
keywords:
  - o-minimality
  - sharp o-minimality
  - format-degree complexity
  - repair-closed systems
  - autocatalytic networks
  - tropical geometry
  - mathematical biology
  - theoretical physics
